1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,624
Throw something away,

2
00:00:01,664 --> 00:00:03,400
and it doesn't vanish.

3
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:04,677
The town's trash piles into

4
00:00:04,717 --> 00:00:06,241
a stinking mountain.

5
00:00:06,281 --> 00:00:07,292
Burn it outside,

6
00:00:07,332 --> 00:00:08,856
and the sky turns black.

7
00:00:08,896 --> 00:00:09,920
So a crane drops it

8
00:00:09,960 --> 00:00:11,396
into a closed furnace,

9
00:00:11,436 --> 00:00:12,460
where it tumbles down

10
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:13,311
a moving grate

11
00:00:13,351 --> 00:00:15,300
as air from below burns it.

12
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:16,364
The heat boils water

13
00:00:16,404 --> 00:00:18,141
in pipes lining the walls.

14
00:00:18,181 --> 00:00:18,779
That steam spins

15
00:00:18,819 --> 00:00:20,256
a turbine for power,

16
00:00:20,296 --> 00:00:21,320
and leftover heat

17
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:22,458
can warm homes.

18
00:00:22,498 --> 00:00:23,522
Lime neutralizes

19
00:00:23,562 --> 00:00:24,786
acid in the smoke,

20
00:00:24,826 --> 00:00:25,424
carbon traps

21
00:00:25,464 --> 00:00:27,113
mercury and dioxins,

22
00:00:27,153 --> 00:00:27,964
and fabric bags

23
00:00:28,004 --> 00:00:29,103
catch the dust.

24
00:00:29,143 --> 00:00:29,741
The white plume

25
00:00:29,781 --> 00:00:30,592
from the chimney

26
00:00:30,632 --> 00:00:32,581
is mostly water vapor.

27
00:00:32,621 --> 00:00:33,645
Magnets pull metal

28
00:00:33,685 --> 00:00:34,483
from the ash,

29
00:00:34,523 --> 00:00:35,122
and the rest

30
00:00:35,162 --> 00:00:36,898
can become road gravel.

31
00:00:36,938 --> 00:00:37,749
Subscribe to see

32
00:00:37,789 --> 00:00:39,879
how more everyday things work.
